<title>HUNGARY: Dunaholding plans unchanged 7pct dividend.</title>
<headline>Dunaholding plans unchanged 7pct dividend.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian financial consultancy company Dunaholding Rt said on Friday its management would propose to pay an unchanged seven percent dividend or 70 forints per share on its 1996 results.</p>
<p>The company will hold its annual shareholders meeting on April 23, Dunaholding said in its general meeting announcement, adding that it planned to spend 198 million forints for dividend payouts.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
